| g | -5.44 in [-6,-5[ | [x]=-6, {x}=-5.44-(-6)=0.56; -5.44=-6+0.56 |
| h | -(2+9/23)=-55/23 in [-3,-2[ | [x]=-3=-69/23, {x}=(-55+69)/23=14/23; -(2+9/23)=-3+14/23 |

For h, -69/23 <= -55/23 < -46/23 proves the stated floor. The negative
mixed numeral -2 9/23 means the negative of the complete mixed number,
-(2+9/23), not the different expression -2+9/23. This ordinary numeral
interpretation is explicit here and introduces no unresolved HOLD.

All eight decompositions reproduce their input exactly with an integer first
summand and a second summand in [0,1[. By the greatest-integer definition,
these constrained decompositions are unique. All inputs are defined in R.

